---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro'
const updated = new Date('2026-08-01')
const fmt = new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-US', { month: 'long', day: 'numeric', year: 'numeric' })
---
<Layout title="Terms" description="The agreement, without the parts that only exist to be unreadable.">
  <section class="py-20 sm:py-28">
    <div class="container-page max-w-2xl">
      <p class="eyebrow">Legal</p>
      <h1 class="mt-3 text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-ink-900 sm:text-4xl dark:text-white">Terms</h1>
      <p class="mt-4 font-mono text-xs text-ink-500 dark:text-ink-400">Last updated {fmt.format(updated)}</p>
      <div class="post-body mt-12">
        <slot />
        <p>
          This page is a placeholder in the template. Replace it with your own
          text before you launch — a legal page copied from a template is worse
          than no legal page, because it describes somebody else's product.
        </p>
        <h2>What to put here</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>What you collect, and what you do not</li>
          <li>Where it is stored and for how long</li>
          <li>Who else can see it, named</li>
          <li>How someone deletes it, and how long that takes</li>
          <li>An address a person can actually write to</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          The style rule for the rest of this template applies here too: if a
          sentence costs you nothing to write, it buys the reader nothing to
          read.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  @reference "../../styles/global.css";
  .post-body :global(h2) { @apply mt-10 mb-3 text-xl font-semibold text-ink-900 dark:text-white; }
  .post-body :global(p)  { @apply mb-5 leading-relaxed text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-300; }
  .post-body :global(ul) { @apply mb-5 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5 text-ink-700 dark:text-ink-300; }
</style>
